gapStatus.evidence:
r12 m2 covers the death grade, the level-up VFX and the kill banners, which were not measured here.

Audio facet: m_level_up, m_self_down and m_respawn exist and fired in the capture. However:
- m_level_up stays silent for about 119 ms (first sample at -40 dB);
- m_respawn reaches -6 dB only at 506 ms (final_audio_verify_files.json);
- nothing changes in the music while you are dead (index.ts:452-474 has only calm and combat).

Confirmed. The cast event fires at wind-up start (src/sim/abilities.ts:276), and hits are voiced on the hit and damage events. All hit cues reach -6 dB within 5.3-7.8 ms of onset.

Some instant-event cues still lag (re-measured):
- c_blink peaks at 186 ms;
- c_cast_shade reaches -6 dB at 185 ms;
- c_summon reaches -6 dB at 306 ms;
- m_ping_vision peaks at 199 ms.

findings.fix:
Give every fighter a sound kit built from VALE's eight synthesized voices plus a home material taken from its own kit fiction. Examples:
- Odrum: a resin/amber crack transient over a frame-drum body.
- Vashil: dawnglass/hourbell partials on his own interval.
- Tunlan: shade-breath with a padded low growl.
- Marund: mortar-stone thuds with hearth crackle.
- Kemdo: heat-hiss FM.

Per fighter, author:
- attack swing and hit, each with 3 round-robin variants (variants=3 in the @cue decorator);
- casts and impacts;
- an ult wind-up an enemy can learn, plus a release;
- a passive proc and a death cue;
- a 2-3-note 'call' on the fighter's signature instrument in D Dorian, for lock-in and ult release.

Name the cues f_<fighter>_* and point present.sfx and hitSfx at them. Keep Wicks and monsters on quieter library sounds.

Add audio/build.py gates:
- no attack or ult cue shared by two fighters;
- at least 8 dB of 1/3-octave distance between fighters' attack and ult cues;
- at least 3 variants for any cue that can fire more than once per second.

Fighter VO is outside the CONTRACT §11 slice ('no voice in this slice'). Schedule it as a separate scope decision.

Keep the tonal announcer the contract specifies and give it a bell language:
- first takedown: one high hourbell toll;
- multi-takedown n: n rising tolls;
- shutdown: falling glass;
- structures: a low hourbell, with your loss over Dsus2 and the enemy's resolving to F#;
- Longshade and Sunsplinter: one timbre each.

Implement r07 §2.2 for the voice bus:
- one sting at a time, in priority bands;
- merge multi-takedowns inside the window;
- 2-4 s expiry;
- duck music -6 dB and SFX -3 dB while a sting plays.

Play one voice-bus item per world event, keeping c_structure_fall as the spatial world sound. A spoken announcer is a separate scope decision (CONTRACT §11).

findings.what:
Fear, airborne, sleep, taunt, disarm and silence all play c_buff, the same soft swell as a friendly haste. Only stun, root and slow have their own cues.

The only allegiance cue is m_enemy_windup:
- it fires only for enemy ultimates within 14 m, although the STYLE_BIBLE says T3+;
- it plays centre-panned, although the cue is spatial;
- it played once in 9 minutes.

No ability has an enemy or ally variant, and the priority lift for enemy sources described in audio.json is not implemented.

findings.fix:
Give each CC class its own sound from VALE's palette:
- airborne: a rising air-glass whoosh;
- fear: reversed shade-breath;
- sleep: a slow lamp-drone sigh;
- taunt: an hourbell knock;
- disarm: a dropped-metal escapement;
- silence: a damped hourbell.

Play CC cues only on fighters, +3 dB when you are the target. Keep c_buff for buffs.

Apply the shade-breath swell to every enemy T3+ wind-up, as the style bible states, spatialised at the caster.

Add the enemy-source priority lift that audio.json describes.

findings.what:
The engine:
- caps voices per cue only, and never reads the declared priority field;
- has no global voice budget (204 slots summed across cues);
- ducks only the music, and only for the ready check, although CONTRACT §11 requires 'ducking (voice > sfx > music)';
- uses a DynamicsCompressor as its limiter, which is not a brickwall.

Heal cues chime about once a second. Part of that comes from lifesteal and omnivamp: every vamped hit emits a 'heal' event.

findings.verifierNote:
Code confirmed. The ducking gap is a real CONTRACT §11 deviation, and the vamp heal spam is a new detail.

Downgraded to minor because the measured harm is small:
- the overshoot is 2 blocks in 541 s;
- the mix balance measured healthy;
- -20.7 LUFS at master 0.8 (-1.9 dB) corresponds to about -18.8 LUFS at unity, inside the tokens -18 ±1.5;
- no 10-fighter teamfight masking was captured.

findings.fix:
Place 4-6 looping emitters per map on the ambience bus, attenuated by distance and ducked in combat, all in VALE's own fiction:
- RIFT: wind over the hour-lines, water in the Noonline, a faint ring in the Standing Shadow, lamp hum at the Lamp Dome;
- BRIDGE: gorge updraft and the creaking shaft;
- FRAY: fair murmur.

Drive them from the map art.ambient points that r12 M14 plans.

